# Deliberately not committed.
#
# A GitHub Pages site is public even when the repository is private, so a
# committed vault.json can be downloaded by anyone who finds the URL and
# attacked offline, forever — and git history keeps it there after you delete
# it. The offline .html backup does the same job with none of that exposure.
#
# If you do want the site copy (a long passphrase, or an auth gate in front of
# the site — see the README), publish it deliberately:
#
#     git add -f vault.json
#
vault.json
